# Cursor Editor — Custom Subagents

## Overview

Custom subagents are specialized AI assistants that run in isolated contexts with custom system prompts. They are defined as `.md` files in the `.cursor/agents/` directory and allow you to create domain-specific agents that the Cursor AI can delegate tasks to.

Custom subagents are distinct from:

- **Built-in subagents** (generalPurpose, explore, shell, cursor-guide, ci-investigator, bugbot, security-review, best-of-n-runner): These are predefined agent types in the Cursor Task tool
- **Skills** (SKILL.md files): Skills modify the main agent's behavior through instructions; subagents spawn entirely separate agent instances with their own system prompts

Custom subagents provide persistent, reusable agent configurations that can be shared with a team (project-level) or used across all projects (user-level).

---

## Custom Subagents vs Built-in Subagents

| Aspect | Custom Subagents | Built-in Subagents |
|--------|-----------------|-------------------|
| **Definition** | User-created `.md` files | Predefined in Cursor engine |
| **Location** | `.cursor/agents/` or `~/.cursor/agents/` | Built into Cursor |
| **System Prompt** | Full control via file body | Fixed by Cursor |
| **Tool Access** | Inherits from invocation context | Defined per type |
| **Purpose** | Domain-specific, team-specific | General-purpose |
| **Sharing** | Via Git (project) or settings (user) | N/A |
| **Examples** | code-reviewer, debugger, data-scientist | explore, shell, bugbot |

---

## Directory Structure

### Storage Locations

| Type | Path | Scope | Persistence |
|------|------|-------|-------------|
| **Project** | `.cursor/agents/` | Current workspace only | Checked into version control |
| **User** | `~/.cursor/agents/` | All projects on this machine | Persists across workspace changes |

### Priority Resolution

When multiple subagents share the same name, the higher-priority location wins:

```
Priority (highest to lowest):
  1. .cursor/agents/<name>.md (project-level)
  2. ~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md (user-level)
  3. Built-in subagent (Cursor default)
```

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Agent needs to invoke subagent] --> B{Check .cursor/agents/}
    B -->|Found| C[Use project-level agent]
    B -->|Not found| D{Check ~/.cursor/agents/}
    D -->|Found| E[Use user-level agent]
    D -->|Not found| F{Is it a built-in type?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Use built-in subagent]
    F -->|No| H[Fail: no matching agent]
```

### Example Project Structure

```
your-project/
├── .cursor/
│   └── agents/
│       ├── code-reviewer.md
│       ├── debugger.md
│       ├── data-scientist.md
│       └── security-auditor.md
├── src/
├── tests/
└── README.md
```

### Example User Structure

```
~/.cursor/agents/
├── code-reviewer.md
├── debugger.md
├── data-scientist.md
└── performance-analyst.md
```

