## Invoking Custom Subagents

### Invocation Syntax

```
Use the <name> subagent to [describe task]
```

Example invocations:

```
# Project-level agent
Use the code-reviewer subagent to review the changes in src/auth.ts

# User-level agent
Use the debugger subagent to investigate the test failures in the payment module

# With specific context
Use the data-scientist subagent to analyze user behavior patterns from the metrics table
```

### How Invocation Works

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Agent
    participant Subagent
    participant FS as File System

    User->>Agent: "Use code-reviewer subagent to review changes"
    Agent->>FS: Check .cursor/agents/code-reviewer.md
    FS-->>Agent: Found (project)
    Agent->>FS: Read file content
    FS-->>Agent: YAML + system prompt
    Agent->>Subagent: Create isolated context with system prompt
    Subagent->>Agent: Execute task, return results
    Agent->>User: Present review findings
```

### Inference from Context

If previous conversation context exists, the agent can infer the subagent's purpose and behavior:

- Reviewing code changes → delegate to `code-reviewer`
- Debugging errors → delegate to `debugger`
- Data analysis task → delegate to `data-scientist`

The agent will automatically use the appropriate subagent without explicit invocation when the description matches the task.

