## Relationship to Other Systems

Custom subagents integrate with Cursor's broader agent ecosystem:

- **[Agent Hierarchy](mdc:02-agent-hierarchy.mdc)**: Custom subagents are invoked through the Task tool, just like built-in subagents
- **[Skills System](mdc:04-skills-system.mdc)**: Skills modify the main agent's behavior; custom subagents create entirely new agent instances
- **[Rules System](mdc:03-rules-system.mdc)**: Rules provide persistent context to the main agent; custom subagents provide persistent context to delegated agents
- **[Hooks System](mdc:09-hooks-and-automation.mdc)**: Hooks trigger scripts on events; custom subagents can be triggered via hooks using `subagentStart` events
- **[Context Management](mdc:10-context-management.mdc)**: Custom subagents receive their own context window from their system prompt; they do not inherit the main agent's conversation context unless explicitly provided

